t-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="JP-9201962-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>JP</country><doc-number>9201962</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit><patcit ucid="US-4176361-A" status="new"><document-id status="new" format="epo"><country>US</country><doc-number>4176361</doc-number><kind>A</kind></document-id><sources><source category="Y" name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></patcit></patent-citations><non-patent-citations><nplcit status="new"><text>See also references of EP     1108541A1</text><sources><source name="SEA" created-by-npl="N"/></sources></nplcit></non-patent-citations></citations></technical-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAMURA TAKUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NIPPON ELECTRIC CO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKUDA MASAKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAMURA, TAKUYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NEC CORPORATION</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUDA, MASAKAZU</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IWAMURA TAKUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>OKUDA MASAKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IWAMURA, TAKUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>OKUDA, MASAKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>Ink stored in an ink tank (11) is filled in a pressure room (14) via a supply path (12) and a supply port (13). A piezo-actuator (15), when applied with a drive voltage by a drive voltage control unit (16), vibrates a diaphragm (17) which in turn changes the volume of the pressure room (14) to eject ink in the pressure room (14) from a nozzle (18) toward a form (2), the diameter of the nozzle (18) being set to within 20 to 40  mu m and the viscosity of the ink to within 2 to 6 mPa•s, thereby stably ejecting droplets of not larger than 25  mu m in diameter and providing a high-quality image. When a drive waveform voltage is corrected in accordance with an environmental temperature detected by a temperature detector (19) to set an ink viscosity to within 2 to 15 mPa•s, a high-quality image can be maintained.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'encre contenue dans un réservoir (11) y est versée dans une chambre de pression (14) par un canal (12) et un orifice (13) de remplissage. Un piézo-actionneur (15) alimenté en tension par une unité de production de tension (16) fait vibrer une membrane (17) qui à son tour fait varier le volume de la chambre de pression (14) pour en éjecter de l'encre par une buse (18) sur une forme (2). Le diamètre de la buse (18) est choisi entre 20 et 40  mu m, et la viscosité de l'encre entre 2 et 6 mPa•s, ce qui permet une éjection stable de gouttelettes d'au plus 25  mu m de diamètre donnant une image de qualité élevée. En agissant sur la forme de l'onde de tension en fonction d'une mesure de la température ambiante effectuée par un détecteur (19) on maintient la viscosité entre 2 et 15 mPa•s, et la qualité élevée de l'image.</p></abstract><